@web-search @feat-010
Feature: Web Search Capability for Player
  As an architect agent operator
  I want the Player agent to search the web for technology research,
  EOL/deprecation checks, and claim verification
  So that conversation starters are grounded in current external evidence
  rather than limited to the contents of local product documentation

  Background:
    Given the architect agent project is initialised
    And a valid LLM client is available
    And the architect role configuration is loaded

  # ━━ GROUP A: Key Examples ━━

  # Why: Core capability -- Player can search the web during generation
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Player agent includes web_search in its tool inventory when enabled
    Given web search is enabled
    And the architect role configuration lists "web_search" in player.tools
    When I create a Player agent
    Then the Player's tool inventory should be exactly {"read_product_docs", "web_search"}

  # Why: Tool separation -- Coach remains at zero tools regardless of web search
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Coach agent has zero tools when web search is enabled
    Given web search is enabled
    When I create a Coach agent
    Then the Coach's tool inventory should be exactly the empty set

  # Why: Core search -- Player can issue a search query and receive results
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: web_search tool returns results for a valid query
    Given the web search service is available
    When I call web_search with query "Keycloak FAPI 2.0 configuration"
    Then the result should contain at least one search result
    And each result should include a title, URL, and snippet

  # Why: Demonstrates the primary use case -- technology research during generation
  @key-example
  Scenario: Player uses web search to research a technology mentioned in product docs
    Given product documentation mentioning "AWS Copilot CLI" without version details
    And web search is enabled
    When the Player generates a conversation starter
    Then the Player should call web_search to research AWS Copilot CLI
    And the conversation starter should include current information about the technology

  # Why: Demonstrates EOL/deprecation checking -- the highest-value gap identified in early testing
  @key-example
  Scenario: Player uses web search to check EOL status of a named technology
    Given product documentation specifying "AWS Copilot CLI" as a deployment tool
    And web search is enabled
    When the Player generates a conversation starter
    Then the Player should call web_search to check deprecation or EOL status
    And the conversation starter should surface any end-of-life information found

  # Why: Demonstrates claim verification -- cross-checking product doc assertions
  @key-example
  Scenario: Player uses web search to verify a claim from product documentation
    Given product documentation claiming "Keycloak supports FAPI 2.0 natively"
    And web search is enabled
    When the Player generates a conversation starter
    Then the Player should call web_search to verify the claim
    And the conversation starter should note whether the claim was confirmed or contradicted

  # Why: Player prompt instructs when to use (and not use) web search
  @key-example
  Scenario: Player prompt includes web search usage guidance
    Given the architect role player prompt is loaded from roles/architect/prompts/player.md
    When I inspect the prompt content
    Then the prompt should instruct the Player to use web search for technology research
    And the prompt should instruct the Player to use web search for EOL/deprecation checks
    And the prompt should instruct the Player to use web search for claim verification
    And the prompt should instruct the Player NOT to use web search as a substitute for reading product docs

  # ━━ GROUP B: Boundary Conditions ━━

  # Why: Just-inside boundary -- search timeout at exactly the configured limit
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Search timeout is 10 seconds per query
  @boundary
  Scenario: web_search completes at exactly the timeout limit
    Given the web search service responds in exactly 10 seconds
    When I call web_search with query "React server components"
    Then the search should succeed
    And a result should be returned

  # Why: Just-outside boundary -- search exceeding timeout is handled gracefully
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Search timeout is 10 seconds per query
  @boundary @negative
  Scenario: web_search exceeding the timeout returns a timeout error
    Given the web search service takes longer than 10 seconds to respond
    When I call web_search with query "React server components"
    Then the search should fail with a timeout indication
    And the Player should be able to continue generation without the search result

  # Why: Just-inside boundary -- max searches per iteration at the limit
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Maximum searches per iteration is 3
  @boundary
  Scenario: Player can issue up to the maximum number of searches per iteration
    Given web search is enabled
    And the Player has issued 2 searches in the current iteration
    When the Player issues one more search
    Then the search should succeed

  # Why: Just-outside boundary -- exceeding max searches per iteration
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Maximum searches per iteration is 3
  @boundary @negative
  Scenario: Player is limited when exceeding the maximum searches per iteration
    Given web search is enabled
    And the Player has already issued 3 searches in the current iteration
    When the Player attempts another search
    Then the search should be rejected or the Player should be informed the limit is reached

  # Why: Empty query string -- zero-length input boundary
  @boundary @negative
  Scenario: web_search rejects an empty query string
    When I call web_search with an empty query string
    Then the search should fail with a validation error
    And the error should indicate that a non-empty query is required

  # Why: Search result count boundary -- tool returns a bounded number of results
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Default result count is 5
  @boundary
  Scenario Outline: web_search returns up to the configured maximum number of results
    Given the web search service has many results for a query
    When I call web_search with query "<query>"
