    Examples:
      | query                                |
      | Python web frameworks 2026           |
      | Keycloak FAPI 2.0 setup guide        |

  # ━━ GROUP C: Negative Cases ━━

  # Why: Offline mode -- --no-web-search flag disables web search entirely
  @negative @smoke
  Scenario: Player tool inventory excludes web_search when --no-web-search is set
    Given web search is disabled via the --no-web-search CLI flag
    When I create a Player agent
    Then the Player's tool inventory should be exactly {"read_product_docs"}

  # Why: CLI flag validation -- --no-web-search is accepted without error
  @negative
  Scenario: CLI accepts the --no-web-search flag on the greenfield command
    When I run the greenfield command with --no-web-search and valid required options
    Then the command should proceed without error
    And web search should be disabled for the session

  # Why: Role config without web_search -- backward compatibility
  @negative
  Scenario: Player works correctly when role config does not list web_search
    Given a role configuration with player.tools containing only "read_product_docs"
    And web search is not disabled via CLI flag
    When I create a Player agent
    Then the Player's tool inventory should be exactly {"read_product_docs"}
    And no error should be raised

  # Why: Web search service unavailable -- graceful degradation
  @negative
  Scenario: Player continues generation when the web search service is unavailable
    Given web search is enabled
    But the web search service is unreachable
    When the Player attempts a web search during generation
    Then the search should fail gracefully with a descriptive error
    And the Player should continue generation using only product documentation

  # Why: Search returns no results -- Player handles empty response
  @negative
  Scenario: Player handles a search that returns zero results
    Given web search is enabled
    And the web search service is available
    When the Player searches for an extremely obscure or nonsensical query
    Then the search should return an empty result set
    And the Player should continue generation without error

  # Why: Tool separation -- web_search must not appear in Coach tool inventory
  @negative
  Scenario: web_search is never added to the Coach agent
    Given web search is enabled
    When I create a Coach agent
    Then the Coach should not have web_search in its tools
    And assert_tool_inventory should confirm the Coach has exactly zero tools

  # ━━ GROUP D: Edge Cases ━━

  # Why: Session logger must capture web search metrics for observability
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Session logger records web search usage per iteration
    Given web search is enabled
    And the Player performs 2 web searches during an iteration
    When the iteration completes
    Then the session log should record the number of searches performed
    And the session log should record the total search time
    And the session log should record the URLs accessed

  # Why: Revision pass -- Player can search again when revising after Coach rejection
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Player can use web search during a revision pass
    Given web search is enabled
    And the Coach has rejected the Player's output with feedback requesting technology verification
    When the Player revises its output
    Then the Player should be able to call web_search to address the feedback
    And the revision should incorporate the new search results

  # Why: Tool registration -- web_search registers via @register_tool decorator
  @edge-case
  Scenario: web_search tool registers correctly with the tool registry
    Given the tool registry is initialised
    When the web_search tool module is imported
    Then the tool "web_search" should be registered in the tool registry
    And the registered tool should be resolvable by name

  # Why: SessionConfig carries the web_search_enabled flag
  @edge-case
  Scenario: SessionConfig includes web_search_enabled configuration
    Given a SessionConfig with web_search_enabled set to false
    When the session is created
    Then the session configuration should reflect that web search is disabled
    And the Player factory should receive the correct tool list excluding web_search

  # Why: Multiple searches in same iteration -- results do not leak between queries
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Multiple searches in a single iteration return independent results
    Given web search is enabled
    When the Player searches for "Keycloak FAPI 2.0"
    And the Player then searches for "AWS Copilot CLI EOL"
    Then each search should return results relevant only to its own query
    And results from the first search should not appear in the second search response

  # ━━ GROUP D (continued): Edge Case Expansion — Security, Concurrency, Integration ━━

  # Why: Search queries could be crafted to inject prompts -- the tool must sanitise input
  @edge-case @security
  Scenario: web_search query containing injection attempts is handled safely
    Given web search is enabled
    When I call web_search with a query containing prompt injection patterns
    Then the search should either execute safely with the literal query text
    Or the search should be rejected with a validation error
    And no injected instructions should alter the Player's behaviour

  # Why: Search results from the open web may contain adversarial content
  @edge-case @security
  Scenario: Player does not blindly trust claims from web search results
    Given web search is enabled
    And a search result contains a factual claim that contradicts product documentation
    When the Player incorporates the search result into the conversation starter
    Then the conversation starter should note the contradiction
    And the product documentation claim should take precedence over unverified web content

  # Why: If one search hangs, it must not block the entire generation pass
  @edge-case
  Scenario: A hanging search does not block Player generation
    Given web search is enabled
    And the Player issues a search that does not respond within the timeout
    When the timeout expires
    Then the Player should receive a timeout error for that search
    And the Player should continue generation without waiting further

  # Why: External API may return unexpected payloads -- tool must not crash
  @edge-case
  Scenario: web_search handles malformed response from the search service
    Given web search is enabled
    And the search service returns a malformed or unexpected response
    When I call web_search with a valid query
    Then the search should fail gracefully with a descriptive error
    And the error should not expose raw API response internals to the Player

  # Why: Missing API key should fail fast at startup, not mid-generation
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Missing search API key is detected at session startup
    Given web search is enabled
    But the search API key environment variable is not set
    When the session is initialised
    Then an error should be raised indicating the missing API key
    And the error should suggest either setting the key or using --no-web-search

  # Why: Search results are per-invocation -- stale context must not leak across iterations
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Search results from a previous iteration do not persist into the next
    Given web search is enabled
    And the Player searched for "Keycloak FAPI 2.0" in iteration 1
    When the Coach rejects and the Player begins iteration 2
    Then iteration 2 should not automatically include iteration 1's search results
    And the Player must issue new searches if it needs web information for the revision
